{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/detectors.py:196` and\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:413` hardcode a `severity` string\n(`\"critical\"`, `\"high\"`) directly into a kernel-shaped finding without ever running through\n`pass3_decide` (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`), so these DET-tier findings carry no\ncomputed `validity`/`impact`/`priority`. The epic is migrating every consumer of `severity`\n(aggregation ranking, the review-bot comment, the `fail_on_severity` workflow gate) onto\n`priority` instead; DET-tier findings need a `priority` value before those consumers can\ntreat all findings uniformly. Both sites already carry `\"decision\": \"block\"` alongside\n`severity` -- only a `priority` value needs adding.\n\n`shim.py::_to_common_finding` (a downstream consumer NOT yet migrated to `priority` -- that\nmigration is a sibling ticket) reads `f.get(\"severity\")` off every blocking/advisory finding\nand maps it via `_KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY`, falling back to `_SEVERITY_DEFAULT = \"medium\"`\nwhen the key is absent. Deleting `severity` from these two DET findings NOW, before that\nconsumer migrates, would silently downgrade an always-block secrets/size-gate finding from\n`critical`/`high` to `medium` in the `review_result` shown to a human. This ticket therefore\nadds `priority` ALONGSIDE the existing `severity` (expand, not contract) -- the sibling\ncleanup ticket (byzantine-spinelike-penguin) removes `severity` last, once every consumer\n(this ticket's DET sites included) has something else to read.\n\n## Approach\nAt each hardcode site, ADD a `priority` float alongside the existing `severity` and\n`decision: \"block\"` keys (neither of which changes): the secrets detector's finding always\nblocks, so its priority is pinned above every configured `block_threshold` (`priority: 1.0`);\nthe bugfix-size-gate's finding is a strong-but-not-maximal signal (`priority: 0.9`). No key is\nremoved by this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `detectors.py`'s secrets-detector finding carries a new `priority: 1.0` key; its\n  existing `severity: \"critical\"` and `decision: \"block\"` keys are unchanged.\n- [x] `bugfix_size_gate.py`'s size-gate finding carries a new `priority: 0.9` key; its\n  existing `severity: \"high\"` and `decision: \"block\"` keys are unchanged.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py -k test_failclosed_forces_block_on_detector_match`\n  (the existing test at line 169, whose body asserts `severity`/`decision` at line 196) and\n  `pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py -k test_oversized_bug_fix_without_attestation_blocks`\n  (line 231, `decision` assertion at line 243) pass, with a new assertion added for the\n  `priority` key alongside each test's existing `severity`/`decision` assertions.\n- [x] `grep -c '\"priority\": 1.0' src/rebar/llm/code_review/detectors.py` and\n  `grep -c '\"priority\": 0.9' src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py` each print `1`\n  (verifying presence, not absence -- `severity` is intentionally retained by this ticket).\n\n## Testing\nTier: in-process unit test against the real detector/gate functions (pure calculation, no\nI/O). Oracle: the returned finding dict carries both the new `priority` value and the\nunchanged `severity`/`decision` values, asserted exactly. The RED oracles to strengthen are\n`test_failclosed_forces_block_on_detector_match` (test_code_review_ws5.py:169, asserting\n`severity`/`decision` at line 196) and\n`test_oversized_bug_fix_without_attestation_blocks`\n(test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:231, asserting `decision` at line 243) -- add a `priority`\nassertion to each; keep the existing `severity`/`decision` assertions passing as a\nregression check that expand-contract left them intact."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788125761468991034,"uuid":"82cfef00-54aa-4902-9659-5dfd1ac87cfd"}